Firefly III on FenrirOS
=======================

Code in /usr/share/firefly-iii (web root: public/). Its .env is
/etc/firefly-iii/env; storage/ and bootstrap/cache live in
/var/lib/firefly-iii. PHP runs as _php. Firefly III needs PHP 8.5 or newer: it runs on
php8.5 (/usr/bin/php8.5, php-fpm8.5, /etc/php8.5), beside the system's php.
Run artisan as _php:
  su -s /bin/sh _php -c 'php8.5 /usr/share/firefly-iii/artisan <command>'

1. Create a MariaDB (or PostgreSQL) database and user for Firefly III:
     CREATE DATABASE firefly CHARACTER SET utf8mb4 COLLATE utf8mb4_unicode_ci;
     CREATE USER 'firefly'@'localhost' IDENTIFIED BY '<password>';
     GRANT ALL ON firefly.* TO 'firefly'@'localhost';
2. cp /usr/share/firefly-iii/.env.example /etc/firefly-iii/env
   chown _php:_php /etc/firefly-iii/env; chmod 0640 /etc/firefly-iii/env
   set SITE_OWNER, APP_URL, TZ, the DB_* settings (DB_HOST=localhost and
   a password of your own; the example's are placeholders) and APP_KEY
   (exactly 32 characters, e.g. `head -c 24 /dev/urandom | base64`).
3. As _php: artisan firefly-iii:upgrade-database
   (creates the tables; run it again after every update of this package).
4. nginx: /usr/share/doc/firefly-iii/nginx-firefly-iii.conf (and,
   optionally, the php-fpm pool php-fpm-firefly-iii.conf, copied into
   /etc/php8.5/php-fpm.d/); enable php-fpm8.5 and nginx
   (dinitctl enable php-fpm8.5 nginx), then open https://<host>/ and
   register the first (administrator) user.
5. Daily jobs: cp /usr/share/doc/firefly-iii/firefly-iii.cron
   /etc/cron.d/firefly-iii and dinitctl enable crond.
